1. Scope and definitions

"Licensor" means Pool Party Labs, solely for material it owns or is authorized
to license. A commercial agreement must identify the contracting legal entity
and be signed by its authorized representative.

"Material" means the Pool Party-authored source code, interfaces, contracts,
adapters, libraries, applications, tests, scripts, configuration, documentation
and original assets distributed with this license, including modifications.
This is the default license for current and future first-party material in the
repository while this license remains in effect, regardless of development
stage. Separately licensed third-party material and the exceptions identified
in LICENSING.md are excluded.

"Official Platform" means the Pool Party services and contract deployments
operated or expressly designated by the Licensor as official. A copy, fork or
deployment does not become official merely by reproducing the name, branding,
source code, addresses or documentation.

"Written Authorization" means express permission in an agreement signed by
an authorized representative of the Licensor. Public source access, a fork,
a pull request, a token holding or silence is not Written Authorization.

