3. Permitted purposes

Subject to sections 2 and 5, the Licensor grants a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive license to use, reproduce and modify the Material, and to
distribute copies only as needed for the following purposes:

a. Reading, learning, research, local testing, and personal or internal
   evaluation in non-production environments, including local or test-network
   simulations with test assets.

b. Security research, vulnerability investigation, and independent audits,
   whether paid or unpaid. This permission does not authorize interference
   with deployed systems or movement of another person's assets.

c. Creating contribution or study forks, sharing patches and submitting pull
   requests. Such copies must remain identifiable as evaluation or contribution
   copies, and may not be offered as a separate operational product or service.

d. Accessing and operating the Official Platform through its documented
   interfaces and features, subject to its applicable service terms and
   contract permissions. Investors and managers may conduct the activities
   supported by that platform, including earning returns and charging manager
   fees. This does not authorize hosting a separate copy of the frontend,
   backend or fund system.

e. Developing and operating independently written adapters, tools and
   integrations that interoperate with the Official Platform. Its published
   interface definitions and integration examples may be copied to the extent
   reasonably necessary for that interoperability. This does not authorize
   copying restricted implementation code into a separate product, changing
   an existing fund's mandate or bypassing platform permissions.

The permitted purposes above include their expressly stated commercial
activities. Paid audits, use of the Official Platform and permitted independent
integrations do not require a separate commercial license solely because they
are paid or revenue-generating.

4. Uses requiring authorization

Except to the extent already authorized by section 2, any use of the Material
outside section 3 requires prior Written Authorization. In particular, without
that authorization you may not:

a. Deploy or operate a separate production instance of the fund system,
   contracts or application, whether commercial or free.

b. Use the Material to offer a separate product, hosted service, SaaS,
   white-label service, managed solution or commercial integration containing
   restricted implementation code.

c. Sell, license, sublicense, rent or commercially redistribute the Material,
   or publish a standalone or modified operational product derived from it.

d. Distribute copies beyond the evaluation, research, audit, contribution and
   official-platform integration purposes permitted in section 3.

There is no automatic conversion to an open-source license after a fixed
date. A separate written license may authorize additional rights.

